// The C symbol a function of the program is emitted under.
//
// Every function is `id_<name>`. A --runtime tree defines functions named after
// the host C runtime's own helpers (print, put, sdiv, list_len), and its cases
// run in a harness built for the build host, which links that runtime: the
// tree's `id_print` and the runtime's would be one symbol twice. So in a
// --runtime build the tree's own functions are `idr_<name>` -- definition,
// prototype and every call to it -- and a name the tree does not define (a
// builtin it uses, a helper it calls) stays `id_<name>`, the host's. The C
// emitter only ever serves the harness there; the object itself is LLVM.

fn_sym(string name) {
  string s = "id_" + name;
  if((import rtc)[0] == 1) {
    if(find_str((import fnames), name) >= 0) {
      s = "idr_" + name;
    }
  }
} return string s;
given edge_fixture given init_rtc ("edge_caller"):("id_edge_caller")
given edge_fixture given rt_fixture ("edge_caller"):("idr_edge_caller")
given edge_fixture given rt_fixture ("not_a_function"):("id_not_a_function")
